Local integration changes:
- Default portable build and optional x86_64 AVX2 companion. Runtime CPU check
  selects AVX2; LINRAD_LDPC_PORTABLE=1 forces the portable implementation.
- --framed local protocol: native uint32 batch length (1..32), followed by that
  many complete int8 LLR frames. Output has the same length and frame order.
  Both ends are built together. Legacy raw input remains batches of 32.
- One-frame batches use a narrow SIMD<int8_t,1> specialization; larger batches
  retain the wide SIMD decoder. Same min-sum-C arithmetic and 25-iteration cap.
- Exact reads/writes with EINTR handling; reject truncated records at EOF.
- Initialize unused SIMD lanes; aligned workspaces also support narrow decoding.
- Skip resetting message workspace when the initial parity check already passes.
- --version reports selected SIMD width; no per-failure log flooding.
- Add --help alias and document framing, batch limits and portable/AVX2 selection.
